This is how i built the internet controlled RC Excavator;

#####Initial inspection~
- Played with it for a bit (obviously)
- Took photos
- Opened excavator, looked at components
- Identified power, radio and controller circuitry
- Took photos
- Put back together

#####First modification~
- Added FPV system, VTX can take 2-6s so direct soldered onto power in(2s). Camera was powered via VTX.
- Used analogue FPV goggles to get good camera position and played with it for a bit
- Plugged in ROTG02 into PC and used ffmpeg to output to a websocket on the Remocon.tv website

#####Second modification~
- Added the Raspi into the mix, gave it power via a 5v BEC
- Grounded Pi to main component board (for signal path around BEC)
- Now came the coding, of which i had no idea how to code. With a lot of help from Remocon.tv, i managed to figure it out;
- Created a excavator_controls.py file on the raspi that connected to a websocket on remocon.tv and output signals on GPIO pins based on keys pressed in the websocket
- I decided on which GPIO pins i'm using and started connecting the wires to the main component board of the RC Excavator
- After a few tweaks to the excavator_controls.py file initial testing was successful
